WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:05.888
The next morning I awoke before dawn in anticipation of our trip to the oyster fisheries.

2
00:00:05.889 --> 00:00:10.729
When Captain Nemo and I went up to the platform, Conseil and Ned were already there.

3
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:16.618
We stepped into the small boat, which was rowed toward Mannar Island by four crew members.

4
00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:22.943
As the sun rose, Captain Nemo ordered the crew to drop the anchor and help us into our diving suits.

5
00:00:22.944 --> 00:00:27.626
Evidently no one from the Nautilus besides its captain was going with us.

6
00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:31.118
"Where are our lights?" I asked Captain Nemo.

7
00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:38.856
"The water is so shallow that there will be enough sunlight to see by," said the captain. "And lights might attract sharks."

8
00:00:38.857 --> 00:00:41.130
At the mention of sharks, I shuddered.

9
00:00:41.131 --> 00:00:48.031
I looked to see if Conseil and Ned had overheard, but their diving helmets were already covering their heads and ears.

10
00:00:48.032 --> 00:00:50.856
"What about our guns?" I asked.

11
00:00:50.857 --> 00:00:55.610
"No guns," said Captain Nemo, handing us each a dagger.

12
00:00:55.611 --> 00:01:01.404
I noticed that Ned was also carrying an enormous harpoon that he had brought from the submarine.

13
00:01:01.405 --> 00:01:06.333
After putting on my copper helmet, I followed the captain and the others into the water.

14
00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:11.507
Fish swirled around our feet as we slowly walked down a gentle slope.

15
00:01:11.508 --> 00:01:17.087
Nemo had been right; there was enough sunlight to illuminate even the tiniest sea creatures.

16
00:01:17.088 --> 00:01:21.674
After walking for about half an hour, we reached the oyster fisheries.

17
00:01:21.675 --> 00:01:29.643
Captain Nemo pointed to the enormous heap of oysters surrounding us, and I immediately realized that I was looking at millions of them!

18
00:01:29.644 --> 00:01:36.976
Ned filled a net with oysters as the captain walked on; he was intent on leading us into a large cave.

19
00:01:36.977 --> 00:01:46.047
At first I could see nothing, but as my eyes gradually became accustomed to the darkness, I could see a huge object on the bottom of the cave.

20
00:01:46.048 --> 00:01:52.880
It was an oyster of extraordinary size, a giant mollusk almost eight feet wide.

21
00:01:52.881 --> 00:01:59.880
I estimated that it must weigh about six hundred pounds and that it would contain at least thirty pounds of meat.

22
00:01:59.881 --> 00:02:03.055
The oyster's two shells were partially open.

23
00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:11.023
The captain inserted his dagger between the shells to prevent them from closing, and then he directed my attention to something within the oyster.

24
00:02:11.024 --> 00:02:16.388
There I saw a single pearl equal in size to a coconut.

25
00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:22.111
Its round shape and beautiful luster made it a jewel of incredible value.

26
00:02:22.112 --> 00:02:28.349
Carried away by my curiosity, I stretched out my hand to touch it, but the captain stopped me.

27
00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:35.262
He removed his dagger, and the two shells closed suddenly. I then understood his intentions.

28
00:02:35.263 --> 00:02:40.016
In leaving the pearl within the oyster, he was allowing it to grow slowly.

29
00:02:40.017 --> 00:02:47.992
Each year the secretions of the oyster would add new concentric circles, and the pearl would increase in size and value.

30
00:02:47.993 --> 00:02:52.572
At that moment I estimated that it was already worth a great fortune.

31
00:02:52.573 --> 00:02:55.738
Our visit to this giant oyster came to an end.

32
00:02:55.739 --> 00:03:03.000
Captain Nemo led us out of the cave, and we walked slowly, stopping whenever we came upon something that caught our attention.

33
00:03:03.001 --> 00:03:10.738
For my part, I was no longer worried about the danger of sharks, something that my imagination had so ridiculously exaggerated.

34
00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:18.397
Conseil walked along next to me, and placing his huge copper helmet against mine, his eyes gave me a friendly greeting.

35
00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:22.381
About ten minutes later Captain Nemo suddenly stopped.

36
00:03:22.382 --> 00:03:26.611
I assumed we were going to turn around and return to the small boat.

37
00:03:26.612 --> 00:03:31.460
But he gestured for us to crouch beside him in a wide crevice in a rock.

38
00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:37.801
He pointed toward something in the water, a shadow sinking to the sea bottom about five yards from me.

39
00:03:37.802 --> 00:03:44.278
My fear of sharks instantly returned, but I had nothing to fear because this was no monster of the deep.

40
00:03:44.279 --> 00:03:49.603
It was a man, a lone pearl fisherman who was starting his harvest early.

41
00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:56.864
Looking up, I could see the bottom of his canoe. He held a stone between his feet to help him descend more rapidly.

42
00:03:56.865 --> 00:03:59.942
The stone was attached to the canoe by a rope.

43
00:03:59.943 --> 00:04:05.093
Reaching the sea bottom, he fell to his knees and filled his bag with oysters.

44
00:04:05.094 --> 00:04:12.349
Then he ascended back to his canoe, emptied his bag, pulled up his stone, and started all over again.

45
00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.762
The diver did not see us because the rock hid us.

46
00:04:15.763 --> 00:04:21.659
As I watched him, I realized that he could not carry away more than ten oysters at a time.

47
00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.690
He had to pry each one from the bank to which they were attached.

48
00:04:25.691 --> 00:04:31.325
He was risking his life by diving, but how many of those oysters had no pearl in them?

49
00:04:31.326 --> 00:04:35.000
I watched him closely for perhaps half an hour.

50
00:04:35.001 --> 00:04:41.746
Suddenly as he was kneeling on the seafloor, he made a gesture of terror and sprang toward the surface.

51
00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:49.317
A gigantic shadow appeared just above him—an enormous shark was advancing on the man with its jaws open!

52
00:04:49.318 --> 00:04:56.468
I was paralyzed with horror. The creature shot toward the fisherman, who darted to one side to avoid the shark's fins.

53
00:04:56.469 --> 00:05:02.135
But he was not quick enough to avoid the creature's tail, which struck him on the chest and knocked him down.

54
00:05:02.136 --> 00:05:05.047
The whole attack lasted only a few seconds.

55
00:05:05.048 --> 00:05:14.968
The shark circled around, and was preparing to attack again when Captain Nemo rose suddenly and walked toward the monster, ready for a face-to-face fight.

56
00:05:14.969 --> 00:05:21.120
The shark noticed its new enemy and made straight for the captain. A terrible battle ensued.

57
00:05:21.121 --> 00:05:28.965
The shark struck the captain and was about to attack him again when Ned suddenly rushed forward with his harpoon and killed the creature.

58
00:05:28.966 --> 00:05:31.111
I sighed with relief.

59
00:05:31.112 --> 00:05:33.524
Ned helped the captain to his feet.

60
00:05:33.525 --> 00:05:41.690
Captain Nemo immediately went to the fisherman, quickly cut the cord that held him to the stone, picked up the man, and rose to the surface.

61
00:05:41.691 --> 00:05:46.023
Within a few seconds, the three of us followed Nemo to the fisherman's boat.

62
00:05:46.024 --> 00:05:51.849
Captain Nemo's first concern was to resuscitate the man, which I did not think was possible.

63
00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:56.777
But after the captain and Conseil worked on him for a few minutes, the man opened his eyes.

64
00:05:56.778 --> 00:06:01.611
Imagine his terror at seeing four large copper heads leaning over him!

65
00:06:01.612 --> 00:06:09.238
And what must the man have thought when Nemo pulled a bag of pearls from his diving suit and placed it in the man's hands?

66
00:06:09.239 --> 00:06:13.262
The fisherman accepted this gift from the sea with trembling hands.

67
00:06:13.263 --> 00:06:21.579
His wide eyes showed that he didn't know what to think of these strange creatures who had saved his life and given him a fortune.

68
00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:27.238
At a sign from the captain, we returned to the water and were soon back at our own small boat.

69
00:06:27.239 --> 00:06:31.246
The captain's first action was to thank Ned for saving his life.

70
00:06:31.247 --> 00:06:38.555
I thought about how brave Captain Nemo was, and how he had rescued a fellow human, even though Nemo had fled from the human race.

71
00:06:38.556 --> 00:06:43.730
Nemo said some chilling things, but this strange man was not completely heartless.

72
00:06:43.731 --> 00:06:56.254
When I mentioned this to him later, Captain Nemo said in a voice filled with emotion, "That fisherman is an inhabitant of an oppressed country, and I will always be a native of that same land."

